  body: |
    # Work in the source’s ESA general rule

    ## Authored interpretation

    For this ESA rule, work can be undertaken with or without expected payment. The source explicitly distinguishes that meaning from remunerative work and qualifies its general exclusion by exceptions.

    ## Scope and boundaries

    DMG 41121–41124 and 41132 separate claimant work, partner work and ESA(Cont)/ESA(IR). Unpaid activity is not automatically ignored, and all activity is not automatically disqualifying: exempt and negligible work need separate consideration.

    ## Inspected source passages

    - [DMG 41121, PDF page 34](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/689db34d1fedc616bb13399c/dmg-ch-41.pdf#page=34)
    - [DMG 41122, PDF page 34](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/689db34d1fedc616bb13399c/dmg-ch-41.pdf#page=34)
    - [DMG 41124, PDF page 34](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/689db34d1fedc616bb13399c/dmg-ch-41.pdf#page=34)
    - [DMG 41132, PDF page 35](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/689db34d1fedc616bb13399c/dmg-ch-41.pdf#page=35)

    ## Evidence and review status

    This is an unreviewed, model-assisted interpretation of selected passages in the frozen DWP guidance. It is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, an entitlement decision or an executable benefits rule. ESA(Cont), ESA(IR), New Style ESA, UC and Pension Credit are not equated. The captured source contains historical, transitional and potentially superseded provisions; no complete or current legal rule set is claimed. Machine extraction can affect reading order, footnotes and characters. No visual PDF review or specialist acceptance is claimed.

